 (e) [Inapplicability to health-care-insurance receivable.] This section does not apply to an assignment of a health-care-insurance receiv- able. Official Comments . . . 2. Purpose; Rights of Assign- ee in General. Subsection (a), like for- mer Section 9–318(1), provides that an assignee generally takes an assignment subject to defenses and claims of an ac- count debtor. Under subsection (a)(1), if the account debtor’s defenses on an assigned claim arise from the transac- tion that gave rise to the contract with the assignor, it makes no difference whether the defense or claim accrues before or after the account debtor is no- tified of the assignment. Under subsec- tion (a)(2), the assignee takes subject to other defenses or claims only if they ac- § 9–403 UNIFORM COMMERCIAL CODE"